// WorldView API · type-check for the code tsconfig.json does not reach.
//
// `tsconfig.json` has `include: ["src/**/*.ts"]`, so this package's 24 files under `test/` and its
// `integration/run.mts` were compiled by NOTHING: `npm run typecheck` skips them by include, and
// `npm test` runs them through `tsx`, which strips types without checking them. A test could
// reference a renamed export, misuse a typed repository, or carry a self-closing block comment,
// and no gate here would say so.
//
// WHY `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` IS OFF, measured rather than asserted. Widening the include with
// the base config untouched reports **58** errors. **54** of them are that one flag against test
// fixtures whose invariants the tests establish by construction — `buildChain([...])` returns
// three rows and the next line reads `chain[1]`, which the compiler must call
// `StoredChainRow | undefined` and which never is. Silencing those needs ~54 non-null assertions
// written into assertions' own setup, which buys no safety and costs review attention.
// The flag stays ON for `src/` (this file does not touch the root config), where an unchecked
// index really can be undefined at runtime.
//
// The remaining **4** errors were real and are fixed rather than configured away: `test/
// liveRoute.test.ts` imported `ws` — a package nothing here declared, resolving only through
// `@fastify/websocket`'s own dependency — with no `@types/ws`, so all three of its WebSocket
// `message` handlers took an implicitly-`any` payload. Both are now devDependencies of this
// package (`ws` pinned to the version already in the lockfile, so declaring it installs nothing
// new).
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: `worldview.yml` carries no `pull_request` trigger — removed by #981 as
// an owner de-gate decision, restorable as group **K** in `docs/restore/`. So this check runs
// after a merge to `main`, like every other job in that workflow. It is a real gate on `main`,
// not a PR gate, and widening it is the owner's call, not this file's.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts", "integration/**/*.mts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
